{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:oriented-unit-normal-iff-pos","title":"lem:oriented-unit-normal-iff-pos","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":1872,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#lem:oriented-unit-normal-iff-pos","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:oriented-unit-normal]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:nonvanishing-top-form-orientation]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:unit-normal]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:metric-preserving]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:adapted-frame-ambient-basis]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"lem:oriented-unit-normal-iff-pos","line":3047,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[One Basis Suffices]\n\\label{lem:oriented-unit-normal-iff-pos}\n\n\\uses{def:oriented-unit-normal, lem:nonvanishing-top-form-orientation, def:unit-normal, def:metric-preserving, lem:adapted-frame-ambient-basis}\n\n\n\n\nA unit normal induces $o(x)$ iff its contracted form is positive on one basis positively oriented for $o(x)$.\n\\end{lemma}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{lem:nonvanishing-top-form-orientation}\n\\sketch A nonzero top form determines an orientation by its ray, so positivity on one positive basis is equivalent to positivity on every basis in the same orientation.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[One Basis Suffices] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a6f7269656e7465642d756e69742d6e6f726d616c2d6966662d706f73\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Aoriented-unit-normal\">↗ def:oriented-unit-normal</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Anonvanishing-top-form-orientation\">↗ lem:nonvanishing-top-form-orientation</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Aunit-normal\">↗ def:unit-normal</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ametric-preserving\">↗ def:metric-preserving</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Aadapted-frame-ambient-basis\">↗ lem:adapted-frame-ambient-basis</a> <p></p>A unit normal induces <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$o(x)$\">$o(x)$</span> iff its contracted form is positive on one basis positively oriented for <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$o(x)$\">$o(x)$</span>.  <p></p><section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Anonvanishing-top-form-orientation\">↗ lem:nonvanishing-top-form-orientation</a> \\sketch A nonzero top form determines an orientation by its ray, so positivity on one positive basis is equivalent to positivity on every basis in the same orientation. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:oriented-unit-normal","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:existsunique-oriented-unit-normal","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:oriented-unit-normal","title":"def:oriented-unit-normal","labe